From 569e29c957632e86b492e61ca98816caa18be793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Cowork)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): extract and delete act on the pages the visitor
 chooses
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both tool pages dispatched `pages: [0]` hardcoded, so "Extract PDF pages"
extracted page one and nothing else, and "Delete pages" deleted page one —
plural promises that could only ever act on a single page. The copy sent
people to the workspace to pick pages, which is not what a tool page is for
(§21.6: the page *is* the tool).

Frontend: an options row on both pages — a page field taking numbers and
ranges in any order (`1, 3, 5-8`), parsed by the new `core/page-spec.ts`
(1-based on screen, 0-based over the wire, §8), CTA disabled until the
selection parses. Extract adds a choice of result: one PDF holding the
selection — typed order preserved, so a selection can reorder as it extracts
— or a separate PDF per page. Two refusals never reach the engine: a page the
document does not have (answered with the real page count) and a deletion that
would empty the document. A corrected selection reuses the document already
uploaded rather than sending the file twice; the cache is dropped on any
operation failure, so an expired guest session self-heals with a fresh upload.
Result rows land in page order rather than network order (split's parts had
the same race), and the page field is dir=ltr so a future RTL locale reads
"1, 3, 5-8" as typed.

Backend: `extract_pages` gains `separate` (schema, `engine.pages.
extract_pages_each`, `documents.tasks`), producing one document per page
titled `<source> — page N`, duplicates collapsed. It implies
`as_new_document`: several files cannot be a new version of one document.

Design contract (gap rule): §3 gains the choice-row pattern — `.cfield` rows
wrapping native radios, since `.seg` is a 36 px dense-toolbar control and this
is a marketing surface with a 44 px floor — and §4's tool-page entry gains the
options row. Also fixes a theming hole found while checking dark mode:
`color-scheme` was never declared, so every native control rendered from the
light palette in dark mode, where an unchecked radio came out as a solid white
disc. Now `:root { color-scheme: light }` / `.dark { color-scheme: dark }`.

Verified: 232 frontend unit tests (17 new), 676 backend tests in
apps/pdf_engine + apps/documents (4 new; engine order preservation confirmed —
extracting [2,0] yields pages 3,1), ruff + mypy + ng lint clean, build + 29
prerendered routes + verify:prerender green, both pages screenshot-checked in
light/dark at 1280 and 390 px plus RTL and the invalid-input state.
data-test parity: 0 removed, 5 added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F23Uqopf6y5UdmLDmxrMGx
